---
/*
  The hero's right-hand panel: what one opencode conversation becomes as processes.
  Every line is a fact from the README (the real spawn flags, the proxied tool list,
  the loopback MCP server's name and the 0600 config that holds its bearer token).
  Static markup, no script. The cursor blink is the page's one piece of motion and
  stops under prefers-reduced-motion.
*/
---

<figure class="occ-tree not-content" aria-label="What the plugin runs for one conversation">
  <figcaption class="occ-tree__cap">
    <span>one conversation, as processes</span>
    <span class="occ-tree__mode">headless</span>
  </figcaption>
  <!-- Lines stay under 50 characters: at 13px mono that is the width of the hero's right column. -->
  <pre class="occ-tree__pre" tabindex="0"><code><span class="r">opencode</span>
<span class="t">└─ </span><span class="c">claude --print --output-format stream-json</span>
<span class="t">   ├─ </span><span class="l">auth </span>  <span class="v">your login, never read by the plugin</span>
<span class="t">   ├─ </span><span class="l">tools</span>  <span class="v">Bash Edit Write WebFetch Task</span>
<span class="t">   │</span>         <span class="a">run by opencode</span><span class="v">, behind its prompts</span>
<span class="t">   ├─ </span><span class="l">mcp  </span>  <span class="v">opencode_proxy over loopback, bearer</span>
<span class="t">   │</span>         <span class="v">--mcp-config 0600, token inside</span>
<span class="t">   └─ </span><span class="l">own  </span>  <span class="v">Read Grep Glob WebSearch,</span>
             <span class="v">your MCP servers, your skills</span><span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></code></pre>
</figure>

<style>
  .occ-tree {
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--occ-line);
    border-radius: var(--occ-radius);
    background: var(--occ-panel);
    box-shadow: var(--sl-shadow-md);
    overflow: hidden;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .occ-tree__cap {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--occ-space-4);
    padding: var(--occ-space-3) var(--occ-space-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--occ-line);
    font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-2xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--occ-ink-3);
  }
  .occ-tree__mode {
    color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
  }
  .occ-tree__pre {
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--occ-space-4);
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--occ-ink-2);
    tab-size: 2;
  }
  .occ-tree__pre code {
    font: inherit;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .r {
    color: var(--occ-ink-1);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .c {
    color: var(--occ-ink-1);
  }
  .t,
  .l {
    color: var(--occ-ink-3);
  }
  .v {
    color: var(--occ-ink-2);
  }
  .a {
    color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .cursor {
    display: inline-block;
    inline-size: 0.55em;
    block-size: 1.05em;
    margin-inline-start: 0.15em;
    vertical-align: text-bottom;
    background: var(--occ-bar);
    animation: occ-blink 1.2s steps(1) infinite;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .cursor {
      animation: none;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 26rem) {
    .occ-tree__pre {
      padding: var(--occ-space-3);
      font-size: var(--sl-text-2xs);
    }
  }
</style>
